# Vigilantia configuration example -- design stage.
# These names are PROPOSED: no application currently reads this file.
# Copy this file to .env for future local configuration; .env is ignored by Git.
# Uncomment and adapt values only when the corresponding settings are implemented.
# Never put real credentials, personal records, or breach samples in this template.
# Copying this file does not start the API or provision AWS resources.
# No environment-file loader exists. Future code must explicitly load and use it.

# Proposed local application settings
# APP_ENV=development
# LOG_LEVEL=INFO
# API_HOST=127.0.0.1
# API_PORT=8000

# Results service (implemented): read from the process environment, not from this file.
# VIGILANTIA_RESULTS_PATH=./reports/benchmark-results.json

# Proposed local paths (directories and artifacts do not exist yet)
# DATA_DIR=./data
# MODEL_DIR=./artifacts
# REPORTS_DIR=./reports

# Proposed IBM Quantum application settings; not automatically read by the SDK.
# Future code must pass these values to QiskitRuntimeService / backend selection.
# IBM_QUANTUM_TOKEN=replace-locally-with-your-token
# IBM_QUANTUM_INSTANCE=replace-with-your-open-plan-instance-crn
# IBM_QUANTUM_BACKEND=replace-with-an-accessible-backend
# Confirm the Open Plan instance and remaining quota before submitting any jobs.
# Use job mode; do not switch to a paid instance automatically.
# Hardware execution is required for the benchmark, not for local simulator checks.

# Optional future AWS deployment: replace placeholders before use.
# AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=replace-with-your-region
# S3_BUCKET_NAME=replace-with-your-private-bucket
# Use the AWS credential provider chain locally and task roles on AWS.
# Do not commit access keys. Local simulator experiments do not require AWS
# or IBM Quantum credentials.
